      "title": "Exception Handling Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Exception Handling Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Raise, Unwind, Run Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "An ==exception== is an object raised at runtime",
                "It **unwinds** the call stack to the first matching `except`",
                "Uncaught: the program ends with a {red:traceback}",
                "`finally` runs even after `return`, `break` or an uncaught error"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "try",
                    "sub": "run body",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "except",
                    "sub": "only if raised",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "else",
                    "sub": "only if no error",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "finally",
                    "sub": "always",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def f():",
                "    try:",
                "        return \"try\"",
                "    finally:",
                "        print(\"finally\")",
                "print(f())"
              ],
              "note": "finally runs before the return value is delivered"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "finally",
                "try"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Matching Clauses",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Clauses checked **top to bottom**: ==first match wins==",
                "List specific subclasses before parents like `Exception`",
                "Tuple catches several: `except (KeyError, IndexError) as e`",
                "`e` is ==deleted== when the except block ends"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Catching Too Much",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Clause",
                "Swallows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`except:` / `except BaseException`",
                  "Ctrl+C, `SystemExit`"
                ],
                [
                  "`except Exception`",
                  "Bugs, but not Ctrl+C"
                ],
                [
                  "`except KeyError`",
                  "Only that type"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Default",
              "text": "Catch a ==specific type== by default, `Exception` at most. Never a bare `except:`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Raising and Custom Exceptions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Raising and Custom Exceptions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Raising and Chaining",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`raise ValueError('msg')` ==raises a new== exception",
                "Bare `raise` inside `except` ==re-raises== the current one, traceback intact"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Sets",
                "Traceback"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`raise B from A`",
                  "`__cause__` = A",
                  "direct cause"
                ],
                [
                  "`raise B` in except",
                  "`__context__`, automatic",
                  "during handling"
                ],
                [
                  "`raise B from None`",
                  "`__cause__` None, `__suppress_context__` True",
                  "chain hidden, `__context__` kept"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Custom Exceptions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`class AppError(Exception): pass`",
                "Subclass ==Exception==, never `BaseException`",
                "One ==base class per library==, subclass it per case",
                "Store fields in `__init__`, call `super().__init__(msg)`",
                "Callers read `e.args` and the attributes"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class AppError(Exception): pass",
                "class DbError(AppError):",
                "    def __init__(self, msg, code):",
                "        super().__init__(msg)",
                "        self.code = code",
                "try: raise DbError('down', 503)",
                "except AppError as e: print(e.args, e.code)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "('down',) 503"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never swallow errors",
              "text": "`except Exception: pass` hides bugs. Raising a bare string is a TypeError. Print-and-continue loses the failure: ==log or re-raise==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
