          "title": "Collections: Counter, defaultdict, deque",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Counter",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Counter(iterable)` counts ==hashables==",
                "`.most_common(n)` gives the top n `(item, count)` pairs",
                "A missing key gives ==0==, not `KeyError`",
                "`+` and `-` combine counters; `-` drops counts of 0 or less"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from collections import Counter",
                "c = Counter('banana')",
                "print(c.most_common(2), c['z'])",
                "print(c + Counter('an'))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[('a', 3), ('n', 2)] 0",
                "Counter({'a': 4, 'n': 3, 'b': 1})"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. defaultdict",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`defaultdict(list)` calls the ==factory== to build a missing value on first access",
                "`d[k].append(x)` needs no key check",
                "Factory: `int`, `list`, `set` or `lambda: 'n/a'`",
                "Reading a missing key ==inserts== it",
                "Test safely with `d.get(k)` or `k in d`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. deque",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`deque(maxlen=n)`: double-ended queue, ==O(1)== `append`, `appendleft`, `pop`, `popleft`",
                "A full maxlen deque drops items from the ==opposite end=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Operation",
                "list",
                "deque"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Remove from front",
                  "`pop(0)`: O(n)",
                  "`popleft()`: O(1)"
                ],
                [
                  "Add at front",
                  "`insert(0, x)`: O(n)",
                  "`appendleft(x)`: O(1)"
                ],
                [
                  "Index in the middle",
                  "O(1)",
                  "O(n)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pick one",
              "text": "Queue: ==deque==. Random access by index: **list**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
